the griffon a legendary creature known  for its recent depictions in medieval  folklore however its origins stretch as  far back as ancient Greece Persia and  Egypt the Griffin has the head and wings  of an eagle with the body tail and hind  legs of a lion the Eagle considered the  king of the birds and the lion the king  of the beasts combining the most  powerful elements of land and sky the  Griffin was considered an extremely  powerful and majestic creature Griffin's  were thought to be very wise and were  often shown God in the gold and treasure  of Kings some legends believe that  Griffin was more of a trickster much  like the sphinx who would challenge  people to solve its riddles the winners  would be allowed to keep the treasure  and their lives the losers would not  this Fink's is similar to the Griffin in  appearance with the body of a lion but  the head of a human there are several  different ways to spell the word Griffin  all of them indeed refer back to the  mythical creature  this variation was used in medieval  heraldry and is a term used to identify  a Griffin that was painted on a shield a  crest or a piece of armor the other  variations identify the creature  directly there are historians who  believe that the idea of the Griffin  came from dinosaur remains found from  the Cretaceous period the pentaceratops  was a four-legged Beast with a beaked  face whose remains were found near gold  veins anyone digging for gold in those  areas could have found the bones of the  pentaceratops and imagine a creature  very much like the Griffin digging and  holding gold the Griffin was commonly  shown to represent wisdom and power the  creature was often painted on the armor  and shields of knights throughout the  ages to embolden them and strike fear in  their enemies even the Gryffindor House  in Harry Potter was named after a  Gryphon with a lion on its crest in  Greek mythology the Gryphon was said to  have pulled the chariot of Apollo the  god of the Sun  Apolo would have to travel from the Sun  to the earth meaning he needed a  creature that could fly making the  Griffon the perfect choice he was also  considered a very wise god an attribute  shared by the Griffon during the Persian  Empire the Griffon was thought to be a  protector of evil and witchcraft what I  find most intriguing is the fact that  Griffon appears to be used more now than  ever the Griffon has become an iconic  character in the fantasy genre we often  see Griffin's and writings of fiction  and movies it's almost impossible to  play a fantasy based game without  finding a Griffon in there somewhere  despite the Griffins popularity they are  rarely mentioned by name  the Griffins lack of mention in  traditional literature means we don't  know much about them they have become  more of a symbolic creature commonly  used in legends and folklore this allows  the Griffon to be very easily identified  but also retains a level of respect and  mystery if you've enjoyed this video  then please go ahead and leave it a like  consider subscribing if folklore  mythology is something that interests  you if you have anything you'd like to  discuss or have any ideas for future  videos  then please go ahead and let me know in  the comments below as always I've been  your host mythology and folklore  explained
 

